/YouGov, the two most recent high-quality surveys, both put her up twelve. Robert Charles has struggled to close the gap, and independent Rick Bennett draws a few points without threatening the lead.\n\nOutside groups have stayed out, and Pingree has roughly doubled Charles's fundraising, giving her the stronger position for the final stretch. Ratings from national observers uniformly favor Democrats, with most calling the race safe. Markets price a Democratic win around 95 percent. The main residual risk is debate-driven movement or late consolidation of independent voters behind Charles, but the polling floor remains high.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9757, "margin": 10.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9716, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9705, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9649, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.961, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9719, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9653, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9728, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9678, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9699, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9727, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.971, "margin": 11.0}]}